# shellcheck shell=sh
# The look of the status bar modules, shared by dwm's dwmblocks / dwmblocksc /
# dwmblocksr and awesome: the separator between modules, the gap between an
# icon and its value, every icon and every colour. Nothing else defines them:
# the scripts print only their values through sb-lib, which adds the icon,
# the gap and the colour, and the bars put SB_SEP between the modules
# (dwmblocks* get it as -d from sb-start, awesome's theme.lua reads it here).
#
# Sourced by the sh/bash scripts and read by awesome's theme.lua and
# sb-claude (lua), so keep to NAME='value' lines: single quotes, no
# expansions; a comment may follow on the same line.
#
# The icons are Nerd Font glyphs. The bars use "JetBrainsMono Nerd Font
# Propo", whose icons are as wide as they are drawn, so one SB_GAP looks the
# same after every icon (the plain Nerd Font gives them all one cell, so wide
# ones run into the gap and narrow ones leave a hole).
#
# After a change: the scripts pick it up on their next run; restart awesome
# (mod-ctrl-r) or the status bar (sb-start dwmblocksr) for SB_SEP / SB_EDGE.

SB_SEP='  '   # between two modules
SB_GAP=' '    # between an icon and its value, and between two parts of a module
SB_EDGE=' '   # after the last module, before the right screen edge
SB_LAST='clock' # the module that gets SB_EDGE (the rightmost one in both bars)

